  "answer": "This crash has been reported before. PowerToys Run throws a NullReferenceException in UWPApplication.Launch (the <>c__DisplayClass64_0.<Launch>b__0 frame) when it launches a packaged (UWP/MSIX) app. The maintainers closed many reports with the same stack trace as duplicates of PowerToys#39090, which is the tracking issue. I found no fix or workaround in those tickets, so the archive can't tell you how to prevent it. Subscribe to #39090 for updates. Until it's fixed, launch Claude Desktop from the Start menu instead of PowerToys Run, and restart PowerToys after a crash. You could also try repairing or resetting the app in Windows Settings > Apps > Installed apps > Claude > Advanced options. Add your version (0.99.1), your log file and the app name to #39090 if you want to help the investigation."
